# Q1. What is a Decision Tree?

# ============================================================

# A Decision Tree is a supervised machine learning algorithm

# used for classification and regression problems.

# Root Node:

# Starting point of the tree.

# Internal Nodes:

# Decision points based on conditions.

# Leaf Nodes:

# Final prediction/output.

# Real-life Example:

# Loan approval prediction.

# ============================================================

# Q2. Gini vs Entropy

# ============================================================

# Gini:

# Faster impurity measure.

# Entropy:

# Uses logarithmic calculations.

# Scikit-learn default:

# Gini because it is computationally faster.

# ============================================================

# Q3. Overfitting

# ============================================================

# Overfitting occurs when the model performs well

# on training data but poorly on testing data.

# ============================================================

# Q4. Pruning

# ============================================================

# Pre-pruning:

# Stops tree growth early.

# Post-pruning:

# Removes unnecessary branches later.

# ============================================================

# Q5. Feature Importance

# ============================================================

# Feature importance shows which variables

# influence predictions the most
